{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_6ue5gm2flz2ujcraoggoemnl65mb7ltpryjp2nipqjlfmfudcj6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both `cargo build` and `cargo test` succeed. Summary of the implementation in `src/chtrie.rs`:\n\n- **`Chtrie::new(n, m)`** — Mirrors `chtrie_alloc`: regulates `n`/`m` to ≥1, checks `INT_MAX` and the overflow guard from the C source, then allocates the edge table of size `(n-1)+(n-1)/3` (filled with `None`) and an empty index pool. `idxmax` starts at 1 (root is index 0).\n\n- **`Chtrie::walk(from, sym, creat)`** — Computes the same hash `(from*alphsz + sym) % ecap` (using `u64` to match the C `unsigned long`). Walks the bucket's linked list looking for `(from, sym)`. On miss with `creat != 0`, allocates a new index (popping from `idxpool` if non-empty, otherwise incrementing `idxmax`), and prepends a new edge to the bucket. Returns `-1` if all node indices are exhausted.\n\n- **`Chtrie::del(from, sym)`** — Searches the bucket. Faithfully reproduces the C source's behavior: when the matching edge is at the head, it sets `etab[h] = NULL` (dropping the entire chain at that bucket); otherwise it unlinks the matching node from the middle of the list. The freed `to` index is pushed back into `idxpool`.\n\n- **`Chtrie::free()`** — Clears all storage (Rust's `Drop` would handle deallocation automatically, but this matches the C API's explicit free).\n\n- **`chtrie_walk` / `chtrie_del`** — Free-function wrappers delegating to the methods, mirroring the C entry points.\n\nThe test in `src/bin/test.rs` (`test_chtrie`) passes, exercising add/delete/query against the same dictionaries as `c_src/tests/test.c`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":526,"cache_read_input_tokens":27393,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":526,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"